codex
Concrete LLVM execution has passed all seven representative cases, including primes, repeated factors, and the prompt examples. The public proof’s generic trusted-claim matcher is taking disproportionately long, so I’m switching to a standard staged-lemma setup: prove the invariant in the base module, then compile its identical rewrite form into a second proof module for the entry theorem.
